WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.980
Welcome to our training on toys and compliance.

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.588
At Amazon, safety is our top priority.

00:00:05.588 --> 00:00:12.665
As a seller in the Amazon store, it's your responsibility to know and comply with all laws and regulations

00:00:12.665 --> 00:00:18.252
and Amazon policies that apply to each of your products, including specific requirements based on

00:00:18.252 --> 00:00:19.370
their age grading.

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:26.075
If you wish to sell children's toys in the United States, we'll ask you to provide certain documentation

00:00:26.075 --> 00:00:29.800
to confirm your products meet applicable children's toy safety standards.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.304
A toy is any item designed for play.

00:00:33.304 --> 00:00:41.565
When selling toys in the US, one of the requirements you must comply with is ASTM F963-17, which

00:00:41.565 --> 00:00:45.283
is the standard consumer safety specification for toy safety.

00:00:45.283 --> 00:00:49.000
We'll refer to this as the toy safety standard.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:56.116
This standard details the test methods for toys intended for use by children ages 12 years and under.

00:00:56.116 --> 00:01:02.442
As the Consumer Product Safety Commission, or CPSC, explains on its website, the toy safety standard

00:01:02.442 --> 00:01:06.000
provides for many different types and classes of toys.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.033
Different sections of the toy safety standard apply to different toys.

00:01:10.033 --> 00:01:16.633
It's your responsibility to know which section applies to the toys you wish to list in the Amazon

00:01:16.633 --> 00:01:17.000
store.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:25.357
All children's toys you list in the US Amazon store must also adhere to the Consumer Product Safety

00:01:25.357 --> 00:01:27.214
Improvement Act, or CPSIA.

00:01:27.214 --> 00:01:30.000
We'll discuss this requirement later on.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.667
Let's look at a few examples regarding the toy safety standard.

00:01:33.667 --> 00:01:39.667
John sells a toy that doesn't produce any sound, so the section of the toy safety standard that

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:44.000
limits how loud a sound the toy makes won't apply to his toy.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:49.667
Mateo sells a toy that contains small parts and is intended for children aged three to six.

00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:56.333
One requirement for the toy is that it must be labeled to inform the buyer that it isn't for use

00:01:56.333 --> 00:02:00.000
by children under three years old because it's a choking hazard.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:06.909
Lee sells a plastic baseball bat and ball set, considered to be a toy, and must comply with the

00:02:06.909 --> 00:02:08.000
toy safety standard.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:14.632
She also sells an adult aluminum baseball bat that isn't a toy but is considered a sports good.

00:02:14.632 --> 00:02:21.632
Sports goods that aren't toys such as the adult aluminum bat won't need to comply with the toy safety

00:02:21.632 --> 00:02:22.000
standard.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:28.233
If you're unsure if the toy safety standard applies to your product or which sections are applicable

00:02:28.233 --> 00:02:33.000
for your toy, you may want to consult a CPSC accepted testing lab.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:41.526
As mentioned earlier, all children's toys you list in the US Amazon store must also adhere to the

00:02:41.526 --> 00:02:42.000
CPSIA.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:48.122
In accordance with this regulation, we'll ask you to submit a children's product certificate or

00:02:48.122 --> 00:02:55.469
CPC from the manufacturer or importer of your toy, as well as test reports from a CPSC accepted

00:02:55.469 --> 00:03:02.000
third-party testing lab accredited to test to the ASTM F963-17 toy safety Standard.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:09.312
Compliance documentation and information must verify that your products meet the requirements applicable

00:03:09.312 --> 00:03:11.000
to your toy.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:19.571
It must also confirm your product was tested to the ASTM F963-17 toy safety standard and any other

00:03:19.571 --> 00:03:26.000
applicable CPSIA standards, such as the limit on the amount of lead in children's products.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:32.750
The test reports must contain images of the tested products, including the packaging, age grading,

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:35.000
warning labels and tracking label.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:40.818
The images of the tracking label must clearly show the names of the manufacturer or distributor,

00:03:40.818 --> 00:03:43.000
the location and date of manufacture,

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:50.385
detailed information on the manufacturing process, such as a batch or run number or other identifying

00:03:50.385 --> 00:03:55.000
characteristics, and any other information that describes the toy's source.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:01.926
It's important to note that the information in the test reports and on all packaging, labels and

00:04:01.926 --> 00:04:06.000
images must match the information on your product's detail page.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:13.043
If you're registered with the CPSC as a small batch manufacturer or SBM, ensure that your SBM number

00:04:13.043 --> 00:04:15.000
is displayed on the CPC.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:22.647
For more information, visit CPSC's webpage on SBM compliance by searching for CPSC.

00:04:22.647 --> 00:04:25.000
gov followed by SBM.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:29.235
Remember to also visit the CPSC website at CPSC.

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:33.000
gov for a list of their accepted labs.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:37.000
Some labs provide special Amazon rates for testing.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:43.562
To find more information about these providers, visit the Service Provider Network page in Seller

00:04:43.562 --> 00:04:44.000
Central.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:50.000
The CPSC's website is a useful resource when listing children's toys in the Amazon store.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:56.545
Here you can find guidance for businesses on what is considered a toy, age determination guidelines

00:04:56.545 --> 00:04:59.000
for toys and other children's products,

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:06.800
a list of accepted testing labs, tracking label information, small business manufacturer information

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:11.000
and other information about children's toy requirements.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:17.125
Information contained in this module doesn't constitute legal advice and is for general informational

00:05:17.125 --> 00:05:18.000
purposes only.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:25.968
Remember that you can find more information on determining if your product is a toy as well as a

00:05:25.968 --> 00:05:30.581
list of approved labs by visiting the CPSC website at CPSC.

00:05:30.581 --> 00:05:31.000
gov.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:37.182
To learn more about listing toys in the Amazon store, search for "selling children's toys in the

00:05:37.182 --> 00:05:37.545
U.

00:05:37.545 --> 00:05:37.909
S.

00:05:37.909 --> 00:05:39.000
in Seller Central."

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:42.000
This concludes our training on toys and compliance.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:46.000
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon store!
